# SPRINT: Search UI — Product Search Feature
# Date: 2026-04-01
# Source: _project/specs/search-ui-design-specs.md
# Target: Fully functional product search — field, autocomplete, results page
# Type: Greenfield feature (Pass 1 → Pass 2 → Pass 3 full sequence)

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SPRINT METADATA
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Sprint Type: Greenfield feature build (Three Passes & Four Layers)
# Pattern: _project/core-building-pattern.md
# Specs: _project/specs/search-ui-design-specs.md
# Grouping: Functional groups per _project/lessons/patterns/functional-grouping.md
#
# Functional Groups:
#   A. Data Layer (GROQ query) — foundation, no UI dependency
#   B. Search Results Page (Server Component route) — depends on A
#   C. Search Field + Autocomplete (Client Components) — depends on A
#   D. Empty State + Polish — depends on B, C

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# LESSONS APPLIED (MANDATORY CONSTRAINTS)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# [CRITICAL] groq-reference-syntax.md:
#   - `brand` IS a reference in productType.ts (line 35-39)
#   - CORRECT: brand->name match $query
#   - VERIFIED 2026-04-01 against sanity/schemaTypes/productType.ts
#
# [CRITICAL] groq-schema-assumption.md:
#   - Never assume field types — schema verified before query design
#   - Searchable fields verified: name (string), brand (reference), sku (string)
#
# [CRITICAL] tailwind-breakpoint-shadowing.md:
#   - NEVER use bare `lg:` for responsive layout
#   - USE `lg-desktop:` and `lg-touch:` for 1024px+ breakpoints
#   - Default `md:`, `xs:` are safe
#
# [CRITICAL] sequencing:
#   - Pass 1→2→3, Layer 1→2→3→4 enforcement
#   - All skeletons first, then all data, then build one-at-a-time
#
# [HIGH] functional-grouping.md:
#   - Complete functional groups together
#   - Data layer → Results page → Search field+autocomplete → Polish
#
# [HIGH] suspense-streaming-components.md:
#   - Create promises in parent, pass to async children
#   - Wrap in Suspense with skeleton fallbacks
#
# [HIGH] pre-flight-baseline-check.md:
#   - npm run build MUST PASS before any changes
#
# [HIGH] type-consolidation.md:
#   - Export shared SearchProduct type from data layer
#   - Single source of truth for search result shape
#
# [HIGH] velocity-aware-sprint-planning.md:
#   - Each SC verifiable in <5 min via npm run build
#   - No re-planning during execution
#
# [MEDIUM] url-state-shallow-routing.md:
#   - Results page uses searchParams (server-read)
#   - Autocomplete uses local state (no URL)

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SCOPE LOCK RULES
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ❌ NO globals.css changes
# ❌ NO homepage component changes
# ❌ NO PLP component changes (reuse only, never modify)
# ❌ NO Sanity schema changes
# ❌ NO tailwind.config.ts changes
# ❌ NO new npm dependencies (use existing: next/navigation, Phosphor icons)
# ❌ NO bare `lg:` breakpoint classes (use lg-desktop:/lg-touch:)
# ❌ NO client-side filtering of search results (server-only via GROQ)
# ✅ NEW files allowed (this is greenfield)
# ✅ Searchbar.tsx modification allowed (enhancing existing component)
# ✅ Header.tsx minor modification allowed (swapping Searchbar → SearchField)

